WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.920
They've got 21 hostages.
Including one child. Lina.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.400
Her father is Colonel Alexis Mayard.
head of the lab.

4
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.120
The mother's in the army.

5
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.600
Looks like they were visiting the dad
at work when the hostage taking began.

6
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.280
The lone terrorist used to work
at the lab. He's an idealist.

7
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.880
He's angry about the weapons they develop
and he wants the whole country to know.

8
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.360
He's unstable and paranoid.

9
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.920
What do they make in the lab?

10
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.200
Don't know. It's classified.

11
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.720
All they told me is it's explosives.

12
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.080
Teams of two. Your usual partners.

13
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.560
Standard rules of engagement.

14
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:52.760
Reasonable self-defense.

15
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.600
imminent threat to a hostage's life
or a direct order.

16
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.680
We know the facility makes explosives.
So hold your fire.

17
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.320
We'll go in through the service tunnel.
Let's move!

18
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.520
Attention all units.
approaching the target.

19
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.480
All units maintain position.

20
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.920
I demand to speak
to the Defense Minister right now.

21
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.720
And I want to talk to a journalist too.

22
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.080
If you don't make it happen.
I'll kill someone.

23
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.696
David and Laurent
in position. Bravo Charlie.

24
00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.600
What's taking so long?

25
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.920
You want me to shoot someone? Is that it?

26
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.000
I'll give you 15 minutes.
After that I kill everyone.

27
00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.280
You hear me?

28
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.920
Fifteen minutes!

29
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.400
You're not gonna trick us
into anything else!

30
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.000
Okay.
I have a visual on the hostages.

31
00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.680
Nothing to report. No apparent injuries.

32
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.600
Do you understand?

33
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.680
Fuck!

34
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.600
Negotiations interrupted.

35
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.200
Fuck it!

36
00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.520
Have a visual on the target.

37
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.440
He has a 12-gauge pump-action shotgun.
There's a detonator in his left hand.

38
00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.560
He looks nervous.

39
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.840
I can't take this anymore!

40
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.400
Stop looking at me!

41
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.760
I've lost Oscar 12.

42
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.520
I can't see the little girl.
I don't know where she is.

43
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.360
Target is on the move.

44
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.240
-Shit!
-He just exited the cafeteria.

45
00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:39.440
Heads up.
Oscar 9 is moving towards the back.

46
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.760
I can't see what she's doing.

47
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:44.320
She just picked up a bag.

48
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.400
What the hell is she doing?

49
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.880
You! Get up!

50
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.800
Just do it! Fuck!

51
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.120
You too!

52
00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.880
She's loading a Beretta.
All hell's gonna break loose.

53
00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.840
We need to act now.

54
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.360
The door could be rigged.
We go through the back.

55
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.000
You too! Get the fuck up!

56
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.640
Get the fuck up! Now!

57
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.760
Shit!

58
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.040
Police!

59
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.240
-Police!
-Stay with me. Amal. Listen to me. honey.

60
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.800
-Target is neutralized.
-You're gonna be fine. Just stay.

61
00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.040
-Sir. we're evacuating. Sir!
-Need to apply pressure. She's been shot.

62
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.496
-Evacuating!
-We'll take care of her.

63
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.240
Keep applying pressure!
Wait. wait! She's been hit!

64
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.480
-Step away!
-She's been hit!

65
00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.976
We have a timer.
Three minutes. Get everyone out.

66
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.360
-Back away. sir!
-Ma'am. can you hear me? Can you hear me?

67
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.880
-Keep moving!
-We're extracting!

68
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.240
Can you hear my voice. ma'am?
We're gonna take care of you.

69
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.040
-My daughter.
-Go. go!

70
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.360
-Move!
-Let go. Did you hear what I said?

71
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.440
Go!

72
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.880
-Your daughter? Where's your daughter?
-She's in the lab.

73
00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.920
-Come on. we have to go.
-Lab…

74
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.080
-She's in the lab.
-She's in the lab?

75
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.160
-The guy planted explosives!
-We'll handle it. sir.

76
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.160
-My daughter's in the lab!
-Get him out of here.

77
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.200
We'll get her. Medic!

78
00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.400
-Doc! Over here!
-I'll find your daughter. ma'am.

79
00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.200
I'll find your girl.
I have a daughter too.

80
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.360
Save her.

81
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.360
Everyone out!
Go. go. go. Get out of here!

82
00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.640
Everyone evacuate!

83
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.520
No. wait!
Hold up! We gotta find the girl!

84
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.080
We're missing the girl!

85
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.240
You've got 90 seconds.
Then get out.

86
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.640
We had almost no time left.

87
00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.240
so Laurent and I
went back to look for the little girl.

88
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.360
Uh… We ran down the halls and. um…

89
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.320
And Lina Mayard died in the explosion
at the lab shortly after that?

90
00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.120
Along with Lieutenant Laurent Villiers.

91
00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.240
Yeah.

92
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.960
Fifteen years ago to the day.

93
00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.320
Can you think of any other details?

94
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.360
Whatever comes to mind
that you could share with us?

95
00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.520
No.

96
00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:05.360
Chloé.
let's look at the wife next.

97
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.280
Right. This is Amal Mayard.

98
00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.360
After her daughter died.
she quit the force and went off the radar.

99
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.640
A year later. the records show

100
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.880
she was killed
in a car accident in Turkey.

101
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.280
The husband.
on the other hand. switched sides.

102
00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.480
He spent ten years in prison
at Bois-D'arcy for arms trafficking.

103
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.040
In explosives mostly.

104
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.400
That's where he crossed paths
with Kröller.

105
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:26.480
He just got out this November.
and no further sign of him.

106
00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:27.960
Not even digitally.

107
00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.480
Through Kröller. he put together
the crew for the CL-20 job.

108
00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.880
We assume he was the one
who eliminated Kröller

109
00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.880
when we arrested him yesterday.

110
00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.800
And he was one of the guys who put
the CL-20 in Chris top he's hospital room.

111
00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.360
I've got half of Recon working on it.

112
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.320
ELITE FORCE

113
00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.600
Listen. it's a beast. You hear that?

114
00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.960
Okay. Come on. Safari Guy. Rev that motor.

115
00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.520
-Watch out. guys. It can get pretty noisy.
-You asked for it!

116
00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.720
-You ready. Max? Not bad. huh?
-A bit more.

117
00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.560
Hang on. hang on. Listen.

118
00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:38.960
-It's too much.
-Again?

119
00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.800
-It's vibrating my jaw!
-Turn it off!

120
00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:41.960
No. no. no!

121
00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.640
-We can't hear you!
-It's making my teeth hurt.

122
00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:45.600
Turn it off!

123
00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.440
Yeah!

124
00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.640
-It's his foot. not mine.
-Whoa!

125
00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.400
Take your foot off the gas. why don't you?

126
00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.960
-I can make some noise of my own!
-Watch out. Max. he means it!

127
00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.880
David. wait.

128
00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:16.000
You getting anywhere?

129
00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.280
There's progress. There's progress. but…

130
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.520
All I really wanted was to be with him
in the time he had left.

131
00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:30.080
You got to be with him every day.

132
00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.880
I won't have that.

133
00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.000
Promise me they won't get away.

134
00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.280
They won't get away. Don't worry.

135
00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.680
I swear to you.

136
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.960
Hey. I've never seen this one.

137
00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:06.200
That was a barbecue at Chris top he's.

138
00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:08.880
But you were there. you know.

139
00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.240
Yeah. I remember that day.

140
00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.200
-I was 10 years old. yeah.
-Yeah.

141
00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:16.960
You know why you remember it?

142
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.560
No.

143
00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.600
You tossed back
a whole glass of wine that afternoon.

144
00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.960
Yeah. I remember.

145
00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.880
-First time I ever got wasted.
-Your mother. she let us have it.

146
00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.400
Oh. we got an earful!

147
00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.160
-Oh! You should have heard her.
-Sorry.

148
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.600
I'm sorry about Christophe.

149
00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:52.280
When I was little. Dad would take me
to the Chinese buffet in Versailles.

150
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.040
It was a thing we did. Just the two of us.

151
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.160
Mom couldn't stand that place.

152
00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.360
I go eat there every year now
on the day that he died.

153
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.840
Usually on my own. but…

154
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.880
Since it's tonight. I thought
maybe you might wanna come too.

155
00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.960
Ah.

156
00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.760
No.

157
00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.280
No. I can't tonight.

158
00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.040
I have to check something.

159
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:31.720
Okay.

160
00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:47.280
Breathing down our necks all day
isn't gonna make us any faster.

161
00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.000
I might have a lead on Mayard. You coming?

162
00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.160
CAPTAIN CHLOÉ LEFORT
LIEUTENANT ADRIEN LEDUC

163
00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:24.160
LABORATORY STORAGE UNIT

164
00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:36.760
MINISTRY OF JUSTICE
CRIMINAL RECORD NUMBER 1

165
00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:48.720
FEBRUARY 10. 2011: TRESPASSING
AT A CLASSIFIED DEFENSE FACILITY

166
00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:01.440
David. I told you when I get anything.
you'll be the first to hear it.

167
00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.040
I thought something might've come up.

168
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.720
Well. I've got nothing.
so off you go. please.

169
00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.840
Can I take a look?

170
00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.440
I guess.

171
00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.080
FEBRUARY 10TH 2010
EDITED: JUNE 30TH 2016

172
00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.040
TODAY. FEBRUARY 10TH. 2 MINUTES AGO

173
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.160
FEBRUARY 10. 2011: TRESPASSING
AT A CLASSIFIED DEFENSE FACILITY

174
00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.000
Where you headed?

175
00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.480
The firing range. you?

176
00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.920
You put your weapons in a gym bag now?

177
00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:48.920
Asshole.

178
00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:51.640
Let me see what you got.

179
00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.040
Do you want me to come along?

180
00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.600
This isn't something
you wanna be a part of.

181
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.080
You know. with gear like that.
it rarely ends well.

182
00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:21.240
Yeah well.
it doesn't always end well.

183
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:08.320
VICTOR DUTEL

184
00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.560
OFFICER LIEUTENANT
LAURENT VILLIERS: OFFICER LIEUTENANT

185
00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.080
Oh. fuck.

186
00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:45.680
I wouldn't have followed you
if you'd just asked me to come.

187
00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.440
You think I don't know where you're going?

188
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.640
It's the anniversary of Dad's death.
We're five miles from where it happened.

189
00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.000
So. what?

190
00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.120
Going to pay your respects?
Is that the idea?

191
00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.640
Go home. Max.

192
00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.480
You know what?
Maybe I'll do the same thing. Why not?

193
00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.480
Don't worry. I won't go with you.

194
00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.240
I'll be there. you'll be there.
but not together. No problem.

195
00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.200
You're right. That's where I'm going.

196
00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.960
But not to pay my respects.

197
00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.280
The man who killed Christophe. Mayard…

198
00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:25.120
He believes we're responsible
for his daughter's death.

199
00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.360
She was killed in the explosion that day.

200
00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.880
I think everything he's done
has been to avenge her.

201
00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.960
Ten years ago.
he broke into a military site

202
00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.240
and was arrested for trespassing.

203
00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.880
The site of the explosion.

204
00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.640
On the same date.

205
00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.520
And you think he might show tonight?

206
00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.240
He just might.

207
00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.000
You came alone to arrest him?

208
00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.840
So you're not acting
under official orders. are you?

209
00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.240
-What are you doing. Max?
-I'm guessing it's an undercover mission?

210
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.120
No. no. no. no. It's not a mission.

211
00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.440
I'm not working undercover.
It's nothing at all. Just go home. Max.

212
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.880
If it's not a mission.
you can't tell me what to do.

213
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.680
That explosion killed that girl
and my dad.

214
00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.920
And you. my dad's partner.
my godfather. my mentor.

215
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.800
you were there when it happened.
and you think I'll stay out of it?

216
00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.240
Here.

217
00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.160
What is this?

218
00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:33.960
It's not registered?

219
00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.240
Don't worry.

220
00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.680
But we're just here
to arrest Mayard. right?

221
00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:47.600
Of course.

222
00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:03.560
It's a ten-minute walk
to the entrance of the facility.

223
00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.120
Remember the riddles my dad used to tell?

224
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.800
Yeah.

225
00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:15.320
How do you flush out a bad guy
who's holed up without hostages?

226
00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.480
Come on. what do you do?

227
00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.800
Just wait till he comes out.

228
00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.840
You're unarmed. So is your partner.

229
00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:34.960
You're held at gunpoint. what do you do?

230
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.440
-Max.
-Know that one?

231
00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:39.160
Yeah. sure. I know it.

232
00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:42.720
You give it your all.

233
00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.200
-You die for your partner?
-Huh?

234
00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:50.560
No. you don't die for your partner.
You have faith in your partner.

235
00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:55.840
You put your life in his hands
just like he puts his life in yours.

236
00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.200
You trust that when the time comes to act
he'll be ready to act too.

237
00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:03.200
The enemy can't fight
on two fronts at once.

238
00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.120
Your faith has to be absolute.

239
00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:08.840
Yup.

240
00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:12.880
Be totally sure that no matter what.
you'll be there for each other.

241
00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:19.040
That's the way it was
for you and my dad. right?

242
00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.280
It was a long time ago.

243
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.600
Breathe out as you hit the water.

244
00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:43.120
Good. now breathe.

245
00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.600
Mind your head. Head up. Good.

246
00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:46.680
Breathe.

247
00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:48.760
Slow measured kicks.
That's it. Keep breathing.

248
00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:50.000
Focus on that.

249
00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:53.640
Stay relaxed.
That's it. go on. Kick faster.

250
00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.000
Come on. tuck your pelvis.

251
00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.640
-Fill up your lungs.
-Major.

252
00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.600
Go on. That's it.

253
00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:03.560
-Major!
-I'm in the middle of something.

254
00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:06.400
-Watch out. you're tensing.
-Commander Berger. Any idea where he's at?

255
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:10.240
-Dunno. He might be training. I suppose.
-Might be training where?

256
00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.120
That's it. PJ. Good job.

257
00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:15.040
Major. it's important. It's about Mayard.

258
00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:18.720
Can you take over here?

259
00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.920
He could be climbing. shooting.
jumping. boxing. munitions training.

260
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.520
We work around the clock.
Could be anywhere. I'm not his mother.

261
00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:37.720
Isn't a section leader
supposed to train with his team?

262
00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:41.200
Normally. yes.
but today isn't a regular day.

263
00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.840
It's the anniversary
of his partner's death. so…

264
00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.920
Does his thing. I give him lots of space.
That's how it is. okay?

265
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.840
If we're done here.
I have a section to run.

266
00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:52.480
Okay. PJ. nap time's over!
Give me another length!

267
00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:55.120
That's good. Fill up those lungs.

268
00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:24.840
The entrance to the lab?

269
00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:26.680
Yeah.

270
00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:47.520
It's David. Leave a message.

271
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:05.600
INTERNAL USE ONLY
DIED IN THE LINE OF DUTY FEB 10. 2010

272
00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:06.680
February 10th.

273
00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:16.720
Shit. February 10th.

274
00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:25.960
Get your team ready.

275
00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.520
I think I know where to find Mayard.

276
00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:30.280
And I think David Berger's
heading there now.

277
00:25:20.200 --> 00:25:21.640
Is this where it happened?

278
00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:26.560
Yeah.

279
00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:09.800
Tell me what really happened here.

280
00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:12.240
What do you mean?

281
00:26:14.560 --> 00:26:18.280
Max. your father. Laurent. died here
and we all have to live with that.

282
00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:19.960
That's what happened.

283
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:21.200
You can cut the shit.

284
00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:25.400
I read the incident reports.
You were the only one with him inside.

285
00:26:25.480 --> 00:26:28.120
Why did everyone
write a report except you?

286
00:26:28.200 --> 00:26:29.920
Why didn't Christophe say anything?

287
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.600
Why no report from you
if there's nothing to hide?

288
00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:37.160
Because I was totally lost.
I'd hit rock bottom. okay?

289
00:26:37.240 --> 00:26:39.720
Laurent was my best friend.
Almost a brother.

290
00:26:40.600 --> 00:26:43.536
We went to the police academy and
did every stage of the training together.

291
00:26:43.560 --> 00:26:46.920
I was best man at his wedding.
I became godfather to his son.

292
00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:52.360
I didn't write a report
because I wasn't able to function.

293
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:54.480
You get it?

294
00:26:56.040 --> 00:26:58.360
I was in the parking lot
before the explosion.

295
00:27:00.280 --> 00:27:03.840
I heard Christophe ask you if you
had told me the truth about my father.

296
00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.320
What did he mean by that. David?

297
00:27:58.440 --> 00:27:59.440
Clear.

298
00:28:17.240 --> 00:28:18.600
Police! Stop right there!

299
00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:27.400
I'll go left!

300
00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:53.840
Max!

301
00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:56.800
Max!

302
00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:01.400
Max!

303
00:31:07.720 --> 00:31:08.840
Max!

304
00:31:15.400 --> 00:31:16.760
Open your mouth.

305
00:31:17.960 --> 00:31:19.160
Ah.

306
00:31:39.600 --> 00:31:40.600
In the vest?

307
00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:44.120
Yeah.

308
00:31:48.400 --> 00:31:50.000
Shit.

309
00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:04.400
I can't picture my girl.

310
00:32:05.120 --> 00:32:06.760
I don't see her in my mind.

311
00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:10.320
This is the only place
where I can remember her face.

312
00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:12.400
See her again. my baby.

313
00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:16.720
Is it like that for you with your partner?

314
00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:19.680
Huh?

315
00:32:22.920 --> 00:32:26.160
-We tried our best to save her.
-No. you stopped me from saving her.

316
00:32:26.240 --> 00:32:27.880
I could have done it.

317
00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:33.600
Do you know what it's like
to lose your daughter?

318
00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:36.280
-I could have taken more from you.
-You okay?

319
00:32:36.360 --> 00:32:37.360
Yeah.

320
00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:03.080
Your dad was a hero. you know that?

321
00:33:03.680 --> 00:33:06.640
He did everything he could to save her.
He gave his life for her.

322
00:33:06.720 --> 00:33:07.800
Shut up.

323
00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:14.280
On your knees.

324
00:33:18.880 --> 00:33:20.200
Cross your ankles.

325
00:33:24.960 --> 00:33:26.400
Hands on your head.

326
00:33:38.560 --> 00:33:41.240
Max. Watch him. okay?

327
00:33:57.960 --> 00:33:58.960
That guy.

328
00:33:59.480 --> 00:34:00.840
he's a coward.

329
00:34:02.200 --> 00:34:05.160
Ever wonder why he got out of there
and your father stayed behind?

330
00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:12.160
You know about
the blast-proof armored doors?

331
00:34:13.080 --> 00:34:14.080
Shut up.

332
00:34:14.640 --> 00:34:16.400
No one ever mentioned them. huh?

333
00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.200
They were activated before the explosion.

334
00:34:20.280 --> 00:34:21.880
From inside.

335
00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:24.040
Only one person got out of there.

336
00:34:24.120 --> 00:34:25.240
That guy.

337
00:34:26.600 --> 00:34:28.840
Which leaves us with only one explanation.

338
00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:33.120
He ran for it and shut the armored doors
to save his own ass.

339
00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:36.640
When he locked my daughter
and your father inside.

340
00:34:36.720 --> 00:34:39.000
he chose his own life over theirs.

341
00:34:54.320 --> 00:34:55.440
Max!

342
00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:57.080
Max!

343
00:35:01.840 --> 00:35:02.840
Oh.

344
00:35:27.840 --> 00:35:28.840
Give.

345
00:35:30.640 --> 00:35:31.640
Okay.

346
00:35:32.080 --> 00:35:34.480
Look at me. Max. Hey! Look at me.

347
00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:37.920
I'm the one who shot him. okay?

348
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:39.800
Are we clear? I'm the one who shot him.

349
00:35:40.400 --> 00:35:41.560
And I was alone.

350
00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:42.640
You got it?

351
00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:45.360
Is what he said true?

352
00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.440
Is it your fault my dad died?

353
00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:50.040
You need to wake up. Max.

354
00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:52.480
The team's almost here
and this is not a sanctioned mission.

355
00:35:52.560 --> 00:35:55.520
If they find out you were here
and that you shot him.

356
00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:58.360
you can kiss your career goodbye.

357
00:35:58.440 --> 00:36:00.000
I don't give a shit about my career!

358
00:36:00.080 --> 00:36:01.480
I want to know what you did!

359
00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:03.080
What the fuck did you do?

360
00:36:03.160 --> 00:36:05.920
Stop being a fucking fool!
Grow the fuck up!

361
00:36:06.520 --> 00:36:07.920
This is not the time to argue.

362
00:36:08.520 --> 00:36:12.240
You're going to do exactly what I say.
Turn off your cell phone right now.

363
00:36:12.320 --> 00:36:14.000
Walk back to your car.

364
00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:15.080
And go home!

365
00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:18.400
And don't say a word to anybody.

366
00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:20.080
Is that clear?

367
00:36:23.720 --> 00:36:25.800
Do it! Now. dammit!

368
00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:27.920
Beat it!

368
00:36:28.305 --> 00:37:28.348
